WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:08.258
ONE MONTH AGO

2
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.512
[bell dinging]

3
00:00:13.222 --> 00:00:17.226
{\an8}KANYARAK BOONSI BORN 1988.09.25
DIED 2017.12.17

4
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:25.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

5
00:00:46.171 --> 00:00:48.090
[Pasin. in Thai]
Why are you eating only that?

6
00:00:48.173 --> 00:00:49.550
You should eat everything!

7
00:00:49.633 --> 00:00:50.926
Mom is watching everything.

8
00:00:55.138 --> 00:00:56.223
Hm!

9
00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:58.350
You're the same. Dad.

10
00:00:58.433 --> 00:00:59.768
You should eat everything.

11
00:01:03.522 --> 00:01:07.818
Dad. let's stop listening to this song.
I'm sick of it.

12
00:01:08.527 --> 00:01:10.445
Why? I want to listen to it.

13
00:01:10.529 --> 00:01:13.115
-Let's listen to Lisa.
-K-pop?

14
00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:17.619
Lisa is not K-pop. Now she's a world star.

15
00:01:18.245 --> 00:01:20.789
You listen to her every day at home too.
Aren't you sick of it?

16
00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:23.458
I'm more sick of your song.

17
00:01:23.959 --> 00:01:24.960
You want to get off?

18
00:01:27.379 --> 00:01:28.964
[Pasin] Long time no see!

19
00:01:31.258 --> 00:01:33.969
[♪ bright upbeat music from radio]

20
00:01:45.063 --> 00:01:47.524
Lisa followed me around every day
when I was in Korea.

21
00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:50.193
[Pasin's son] Oh! You're lying again.
You're such a liar!

22
00:01:51.486 --> 00:01:52.904
You want me to call her?

23
00:01:52.988 --> 00:01:58.660
Yeah. call her. I said. call her.
Call her now. Yeah. call her.

24
00:02:03.498 --> 00:02:05.375
[vehicles approaching]

25
00:02:10.213 --> 00:02:12.299
[♪ ominous music playing]

26
00:02:29.066 --> 00:02:31.151
[♪ intense action music playing]

27
00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:33.278
[both grunting]

28
00:02:42.537 --> 00:02:44.331
[both grunting]

29
00:02:44.414 --> 00:02:45.499
[thuds]

30
00:02:52.089 --> 00:02:53.548
[mercenary] Go! Go! Go!

31
00:02:54.091 --> 00:02:56.301
[♪ intense action music continues]

32
00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:05.602
[thuds]

33
00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:13.235
[in English] Hey. we need to borrow
your dad for a bit.

34
00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:16.154
[Pasin's son breathing shakily]

35
00:03:17.656 --> 00:03:18.657
[in Thai] It's okay.

36
00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:22.786
Don't be scared. Atti.

37
00:03:26.415 --> 00:03:33.422
A SHOP FOR KILLERS 2

38
00:03:37.426 --> 00:03:39.845
EPISODE 06
THE TROJAN HORSE

39
00:03:39.928 --> 00:03:44.141
[announcer. in English]
<i>Three-nine. two-zero. five-zero.</i>

40
00:03:44.933 --> 00:03:47.644
<i>seven-seven. three-four…</i>

41
00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:49.229
[Jinman] K.

42
00:03:51.773 --> 00:03:54.818
[♪ tense music playing]

43
00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:57.320
WILL ARRIVE AT 11:00 AM LOCAL TIME
IN THAILAND. CONTACT PASIN.

44
00:03:57.404 --> 00:03:59.906
REQUEST ATTI'S LOCATION AND
THE KIDNAPPERS' INFORMATION BY 11:00

45
00:04:00.031 --> 00:04:02.659
[sighs] This is how the mole e-mails.

46
00:04:04.119 --> 00:04:05.787
When I'm in Thailand.
I'll be communicating

47
00:04:05.871 --> 00:04:06.955
with the mole like this.

48
00:04:07.038 --> 00:04:08.540
so verify the information.

49
00:04:09.666 --> 00:04:11.042
[Jinwoo] That wasn't easy.

50
00:04:12.169 --> 00:04:15.255
But it came out nicely.
Passport and satellite phone.

51
00:04:15.338 --> 00:04:16.673
REPUBLIC OF KOREA PASSPORT
CHOI. MYUNG GYU

52
00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:18.383
What's this? You're going in alone?

53
00:04:19.468 --> 00:04:21.511
You're not going to take Jinwoo
or Cheolseung in there?

54
00:04:22.387 --> 00:04:25.515
Hey. it's Pasin.
The two of us together will be fine.

55
00:04:26.641 --> 00:04:27.726
I just…

56
00:04:27.809 --> 00:04:29.144
Think about it. Jeong Jian.

57
00:04:29.978 --> 00:04:31.354
We made our deal already.

58
00:04:31.438 --> 00:04:33.356
but they still went ahead
and grabbed his son.

59
00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:35.859
That means Babylon's planning
something else.

60
00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:38.904
If the shopping mall's unguarded
while we're away.

61
00:04:38.987 --> 00:04:40.906
they might use that opening to attack.

62
00:04:40.989 --> 00:04:43.241
We need to leave some of you behind.

63
00:04:45.619 --> 00:04:46.661
[satellite phone beeps]

64
00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:50.248
[Cheolseung] This satellite phone
doesn't have a delay. does it?

65
00:04:50.332 --> 00:04:52.709
[Jinwoo] No. it works right away.
Only on this channel.

66
00:04:53.376 --> 00:04:55.962
[♪ tense music continues]

67
00:05:03.553 --> 00:05:05.305
Are you sure about going alone like this?

68
00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:08.892
[sighs] Don't you think it's safer
if I tagged along?

69
00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:12.020
No. stay here.
Jian's going to need you more with her.

70
00:05:15.524 --> 00:05:17.108
[engine revving]

71
00:05:34.417 --> 00:05:35.627
[sighs softly]

72
00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:38.338
[Jinman] Listen up. Jeong Jian.

73
00:05:39.631 --> 00:05:42.259
There could be a situation
where you lose an arm.

74
00:05:43.927 --> 00:05:45.053
What happens then?

75
00:05:45.136 --> 00:05:46.930
Don't try to recover the arm you lost.

76
00:05:48.557 --> 00:05:50.600
You should protect the one you still have.

77
00:05:52.394 --> 00:05:54.855
[♪ tense music continues]

78
00:06:05.866 --> 00:06:07.659
[engine starting. revving]

79
00:06:30.807 --> 00:06:32.767
[♪ low pensive music playing]

80
00:07:10.305 --> 00:07:13.308
[Pasin] <i>Khao Lak Center.</i>
<i>locker number eight.</i>

81
00:07:14.184 --> 00:07:17.145
<i>Password is 2-4-5-1.</i>

82
00:07:19.147 --> 00:07:20.815
<i>You can find a device inside.</i>

83
00:07:22.108 --> 00:07:24.611
<i>The coordinates will take you</i>
<i>to an Internet café.</i>

84
00:07:25.862 --> 00:07:27.197
<i>I'll meet you there.</i>

85
00:07:28.698 --> 00:07:31.409
[♪ tense music playing]

86
00:07:41.711 --> 00:07:43.338
[phone clattering]

87
00:08:04.943 --> 00:08:06.111
[♪ music fades]

88
00:08:06.194 --> 00:08:09.280
[indistinct chatter]

89
00:08:13.702 --> 00:08:15.662
[in Thai] Pay later. Sit.
You can use the seat over there.

90
00:08:16.162 --> 00:08:17.455
-[Jinman] There?
-Yeah.

91
00:08:23.378 --> 00:08:25.422
Hey! Why are you cheating?

92
00:08:25.505 --> 00:08:28.216
[gamer] What cheating? You crazy bastard.

93
00:08:28.967 --> 00:08:31.761
[indistinct chatter continues]

94
00:08:58.371 --> 00:09:00.999
[drone buzzing]

95
00:09:11.926 --> 00:09:14.554
[♪ low tense music playing]

96
00:09:16.890 --> 00:09:19.726
[patrons complaining indistinctly]

97
00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:33.531
[blade scraping]

98
00:09:48.838 --> 00:09:52.092
[attackers grunting]

99
00:09:57.597 --> 00:09:59.474
[screams]

100
00:10:02.977 --> 00:10:05.772
[♪ low suspenseful music playing]

101
00:10:07.232 --> 00:10:08.608
[attackers yelping]

102
00:10:15.949 --> 00:10:17.075
It's just him anyway.

103
00:10:18.618 --> 00:10:19.619
Get him!

104
00:10:19.911 --> 00:10:22.247
[attackers screaming]

105
00:10:26.835 --> 00:10:30.713
[Pasin panting]

106
00:10:36.136 --> 00:10:38.012
[groans]

107
00:10:48.606 --> 00:10:50.358
[glass shatters]

108
00:10:58.074 --> 00:11:00.493
[♪ tense music playing]

109
00:11:03.955 --> 00:11:06.499
[taser zapping]

110
00:11:14.966 --> 00:11:17.552
-[taser zapping]
-[groans softly]

111
00:11:23.266 --> 00:11:25.977
[mercenary whistling]

112
00:11:29.731 --> 00:11:31.608
[in English] Whoa… Two of them.

113
00:11:32.442 --> 00:11:33.610
Still holding out.

114
00:11:34.569 --> 00:11:36.696
Really haven't changed at all.
have you. Jinman?

115
00:11:37.697 --> 00:11:38.740
[bat thudding]

116
00:11:43.369 --> 00:11:45.830
[alarm beeping softly]

117
00:11:51.544 --> 00:11:52.545
Huh?

118
00:12:01.763 --> 00:12:02.972
[gasps]

119
00:12:07.894 --> 00:12:10.605
[♪ lingering ominous music playing]

120
00:12:19.322 --> 00:12:22.367
[Jin] <i>Did you really think</i>
<i>that Babylon couldn't find you?</i>

121
00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:25.620
-[blows thudding]
-[Pasin groaning]

122
00:12:30.458 --> 00:12:32.252
[Jin] I really do hate it.

123
00:12:34.379 --> 00:12:35.797
The smell of blood.

124
00:12:35.922 --> 00:12:37.257
[sniffs. groans in disgust]

125
00:12:37.423 --> 00:12:38.633
The smell of sweat.

126
00:12:40.301 --> 00:12:42.011
[roars angrily]

127
00:12:42.303 --> 00:12:44.847
I'll break your neck!

128
00:12:46.432 --> 00:12:50.436
Family… is always the problem.

129
00:12:51.813 --> 00:12:53.606
You know. in the past.

130
00:12:53.690 --> 00:12:57.527
they used to exterminate three generations

131
00:12:57.610 --> 00:13:00.613
just to prevent
any uncertain future revenge.

132
00:13:01.364 --> 00:13:03.658
Seems quite reasonable
when you think about it.

133
00:13:04.742 --> 00:13:06.744
But it's really too bad.

134
00:13:06.828 --> 00:13:08.329
People can't do that anymore.

135
00:13:08.413 --> 00:13:09.747
Where's Atti?

136
00:13:09.831 --> 00:13:10.957
[in Thai] You bitch!

137
00:13:11.207 --> 00:13:12.917
[shushing]

138
00:13:14.502 --> 00:13:16.462
[Pasin groans]

139
00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:25.388
[in English] Turns out your son
has leukemia.

140
00:13:26.014 --> 00:13:27.473
[Pasin grunts]

141
00:13:36.357 --> 00:13:38.693
[Jin] It's really remarkable.

142
00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:45.908
You poured all the money you made
for a decade into your son.

143
00:13:52.707 --> 00:13:53.708
[grunts]

144
00:14:01.174 --> 00:14:02.175
[spits]

145
00:14:06.137 --> 00:14:07.847
[Pasin] Babylon!

146
00:14:08.848 --> 00:14:10.266
You listen now.

147
00:14:11.809 --> 00:14:14.395
Anything happens to Atti…

148
00:14:16.856 --> 00:14:19.358
you all die.

149
00:14:20.234 --> 00:14:23.654
Do not waste your time
thinking about killing me.

150
00:14:24.197 --> 00:14:27.033
You should be thinking
about saving your son.

151
00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:29.786
[♪ ominous music playing]

152
00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:32.246
[gun cocking]

153
00:14:36.751 --> 00:14:38.252
[gunshot ringing]

154
00:14:38.836 --> 00:14:40.546
-[groans]
-[K] Good work.

155
00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:42.131
[Jin] Don't worry.

156
00:14:43.174 --> 00:14:45.218
We're taking good care of him.

157
00:14:49.722 --> 00:14:51.682
So in return…

158
00:14:53.059 --> 00:14:55.812
you are going to have to do
a little work for us.

159
00:14:56.979 --> 00:14:58.940
[groans]

160
00:15:05.988 --> 00:15:08.741
[howls in pain]

161
00:15:09.408 --> 00:15:10.868
[Pasin] Atti.

162
00:15:19.085 --> 00:15:20.711
So you're saying…

163
00:15:21.754 --> 00:15:23.631
you never met my uncle there. then?

164
00:15:24.632 --> 00:15:27.552
[♪ pensive music playing]

165
00:15:29.470 --> 00:15:30.888
-[staple gun clicking]
-[Pasin groans]

166
00:15:32.890 --> 00:15:33.891
Ah. Ah.

167
00:15:33.975 --> 00:15:36.894
-[K] <i>Can you hear me?</i>
-I hear you.

168
00:15:37.562 --> 00:15:38.938
Loud and clear.

169
00:15:43.484 --> 00:15:45.611
We are listening to everything you say.

170
00:15:46.779 --> 00:15:48.906
[Jin] Don't try anything fucking stupid.

171
00:15:50.283 --> 00:15:53.911
If you do. your Atti won't be safe.

172
00:15:56.497 --> 00:15:58.666
About 12 hours ago.

173
00:15:58.749 --> 00:16:01.460
Jinman showed me the messages
that he got from the mole.

174
00:16:02.753 --> 00:16:06.424
[♪ pensive music playing]

175
00:16:16.392 --> 00:16:19.103
{\an8}[Pasin] Once I got into Korea.
I went to that address

176
00:16:20.229 --> 00:16:21.480
and got ambushed.

177
00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:25.651
Pasin?

178
00:16:27.945 --> 00:16:29.322
-[Pasin groans]
-[Brother chuckles softly]

179
00:16:30.907 --> 00:16:35.161
[Jian] My uncle goes missing in Thailand.
and Master Pasin gets ambushed here.

180
00:16:35.786 --> 00:16:37.914
And the two of them never even met up.

181
00:16:38.956 --> 00:16:41.375
What about the message master received.
is it legit?

182
00:16:41.459 --> 00:16:43.628
There are only a few people
who know the random combinations

183
00:16:43.711 --> 00:16:45.963
and to change the e-mail every 12 hours.

184
00:16:46.047 --> 00:16:49.550
Captain Jinman. the mole.
and then just us.

185
00:16:51.135 --> 00:16:53.137
And unless someone in here leaked it.

186
00:16:53.221 --> 00:16:55.932
there's no way the information
we're getting is compromised.

187
00:16:58.643 --> 00:17:01.562
[sighs] Why can't I get in touch
with my uncle. then?

188
00:17:09.987 --> 00:17:12.907
[♪ tense music playing]

189
00:17:22.208 --> 00:17:25.086
Huh? What's up? You all right?

190
00:17:25.169 --> 00:17:26.545
You should rest longer.

191
00:17:27.255 --> 00:17:28.673
This won't kill me.

192
00:17:30.758 --> 00:17:32.343
You just scan your hand here?

193
00:17:32.468 --> 00:17:34.845
Ah. Wanna go up there?

194
00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:52.196
Officer Jinwoo.
you're still working at the station?

195
00:17:52.280 --> 00:17:54.574
Actually. I quit the police for now.

196
00:17:54.657 --> 00:17:55.992
[chuckles]

197
00:17:58.244 --> 00:17:59.829
You should just stay there.

198
00:18:01.163 --> 00:18:02.623
It suits you better.

199
00:18:04.584 --> 00:18:09.088
After being ambushed by Babylon.
seems like a bitter fit for me here.

200
00:18:09.922 --> 00:18:12.383
And I should stay where I'm needed.
don't you think?

201
00:18:13.759 --> 00:18:17.013
I was just… wasting away.

202
00:18:17.638 --> 00:18:20.766
A police station out in the sticks?
Nothing happens out there.

203
00:18:22.643 --> 00:18:24.979
[♪ tense music continues]

204
00:18:30.443 --> 00:18:34.280
This was actually a grain dryer.
Brother turned it into an elevator.

205
00:18:35.114 --> 00:18:37.617
[Jinwoo] That little punk keeps evolving
down in the basement.

206
00:18:51.631 --> 00:18:53.758
You wouldn't believe what we went through.

207
00:18:53.841 --> 00:18:55.843
It was hell getting this place
up and running.

208
00:18:58.262 --> 00:19:00.723
Code Reds and Code Yellows
really helped us out.

209
00:19:00.806 --> 00:19:02.350
Couldn't have done it without them.

210
00:19:05.519 --> 00:19:08.856
We open the doors at 10:00
and close at 1900.

211
00:19:08.939 --> 00:19:12.568
And then everyone goes home.
Quiet. not a single person's here.

212
00:19:12.652 --> 00:19:14.278
It's perfect for what we're doing.

213
00:19:16.864 --> 00:19:20.534
[Pasin] Everyone here.
are they all civilians?

214
00:19:20.618 --> 00:19:22.453
It covers for us. for sure.

215
00:19:23.412 --> 00:19:24.955
No one would suspect it.

216
00:19:26.165 --> 00:19:27.208
[visitor] President Park!

217
00:19:28.292 --> 00:19:31.087
-Hi. President Choi. How are you?
-Could you come over here?

218
00:19:32.755 --> 00:19:35.758
[Jinwoo] Hey. I'm the president.
I'll be back.

219
00:19:37.468 --> 00:19:40.388
President Choi.
you're coming by so early again.

220
00:19:41.972 --> 00:19:43.474
You're killing me here. really!

221
00:19:44.684 --> 00:19:47.061
[staff] I'll look at it later.
I'll look at it later.

222
00:19:47.144 --> 00:19:49.230
No. no. no.
I'll look at it later. all right?

223
00:19:52.942 --> 00:19:53.943
Oh?

224
00:19:55.027 --> 00:19:57.863
[in Thai] Are you Thai? Eat some of this.

225
00:19:58.531 --> 00:20:01.951
It's not as good as the one back home.
but we can eat it well enough.

226
00:20:02.660 --> 00:20:03.661
I'm fine.

227
00:20:03.744 --> 00:20:06.288
Pasin. why are you standing there
like an idiot?

228
00:20:06.372 --> 00:20:07.915
Take this and go to the toilet.

229
00:20:10.584 --> 00:20:11.836
Babylon is watching everything.

230
00:20:11.919 --> 00:20:16.507
If you want to keep Atti alive.
don't try any funny business. Take it.

231
00:20:16.590 --> 00:20:18.592
[in English] Thanks for everything. man.

232
00:20:20.594 --> 00:20:23.264
[♪ music warping]

233
00:20:37.653 --> 00:20:39.989
[faucet running]

234
00:21:08.309 --> 00:21:09.351
You take a shit?

235
00:21:10.311 --> 00:21:11.812
Why'd you disappear like that?

236
00:21:16.484 --> 00:21:19.361
Don't worry too much about Atti.
Nothing's gonna happen.

237
00:21:20.613 --> 00:21:23.616
Make a full recovery first.
Then you can find him.

238
00:21:24.408 --> 00:21:27.411
[♪ tense pensive music playing]

239
00:22:04.782 --> 00:22:07.952
Master! Are you feeling better?

240
00:22:08.619 --> 00:22:12.540
-Anything on Jinman?
-No. Not yet.

241
00:22:13.499 --> 00:22:15.376
How about the mole? Anything?

242
00:22:21.215 --> 00:22:24.218
[♪ ominous music playing]

243
00:22:46.323 --> 00:22:48.284
[Brother] Want to go down
to the shopping mall?

244
00:22:49.952 --> 00:22:54.874
Unlike going to the outside.
you need one other thing to get in there.

245
00:23:00.045 --> 00:23:01.505
[machine beeping]

246
00:23:11.181 --> 00:23:14.643
The shopping mall has gotten twice as big.

247
00:23:14.727 --> 00:23:19.982
That also means twice as much work.
but Jinwoo and Jeong Jian help out a lot.

248
00:23:20.065 --> 00:23:23.319
Here I don't even have
to drive a forklift.

249
00:23:24.028 --> 00:23:27.281
If something goes wrong.
is there an escape route?

250
00:23:33.787 --> 00:23:35.039
Of course there is.

251
00:23:35.956 --> 00:23:39.627
<i>But the location is a secret</i>
<i>that only the security manager knows.</i>

252
00:23:40.377 --> 00:23:43.047
<i>Because until recently.</i>
<i>a fake murthehelp app was out there.</i>

253
00:23:43.130 --> 00:23:45.633
The… the dumbass with the stutter is…

254
00:23:47.051 --> 00:23:48.302
that one. isn't he?

255
00:23:48.385 --> 00:23:50.554
[Brother] <i>We lost a lot of clients</i>
<i>because of them.</i>

256
00:23:50.638 --> 00:23:52.723
but we got a lot of them back now.

257
00:23:54.516 --> 00:23:57.770
[♪ tense pensive music playing]

258
00:23:58.771 --> 00:24:00.147
Oh.

259
00:24:02.066 --> 00:24:03.067
Check this out.

260
00:24:04.276 --> 00:24:05.736
Jeong Jian. [chuckles]

261
00:24:05.819 --> 00:24:08.614
Uh… My butt gets sweaty
so she got this for me.

262
00:24:10.032 --> 00:24:12.201
It feels cool. It's nice and dry.

263
00:24:14.036 --> 00:24:17.581
Murthehelp looks like a tight operation
that's so thorough.

264
00:24:17.665 --> 00:24:19.208
then you see things like this.

265
00:24:19.291 --> 00:24:21.335
[Brother] <i>She even bought me two.</i>
<i>in case I need one later.</i>

266
00:24:21.418 --> 00:24:23.963
It's just a gaggle of freaks
that are in there.

267
00:24:24.046 --> 00:24:26.423
[Brother] <i>But she still treats me</i>
<i>like a kid.</i>

268
00:24:26.507 --> 00:24:28.968
[Jin] Is this stuttering fool
really the brains?

269
00:24:30.219 --> 00:24:31.470
Should I just kill him?

270
00:24:36.850 --> 00:24:38.227
[sighs]

271
00:24:38.686 --> 00:24:42.815
How many times do I have to tell you?
Don't you know how to knock?

272
00:24:42.898 --> 00:24:45.985
Oh. I did.
I just didn't hear an answer. so I…

273
00:24:47.152 --> 00:24:49.571
I'll make sure
that I knock louder next time. miss.

274
00:24:52.408 --> 00:24:53.409
Why are you here?

275
00:24:53.492 --> 00:24:58.497
Uh. I'm here about the bus explosion.
Shouldn't we investigate it?

276
00:25:02.126 --> 00:25:04.628
I was looking over the victims'
families' insurance claims

277
00:25:04.712 --> 00:25:05.963
and I started thinking…

278
00:25:06.714 --> 00:25:09.633
it could've been an attack on us
from Jeong Jinman's side.

279
00:25:09.717 --> 00:25:12.302
In that case.
I think we should make preparations.

280
00:25:12.386 --> 00:25:15.264
We should have some contingencies.

281
00:25:15.347 --> 00:25:18.100
Things like this shouldn't happen here.
isn't that right?

282
00:25:18.183 --> 00:25:23.939
Babylon's image is at risk. and it's just.
the employees are feeling really anxious.

283
00:25:24.023 --> 00:25:26.734
The audit team is still investigating. no?

284
00:25:27.860 --> 00:25:29.486
[Inseop] Yes. well. that's true. but…

285
00:25:31.864 --> 00:25:33.574
Then let's just wait a bit longer.

286
00:25:34.825 --> 00:25:36.910
Preparedness is a constant state.

287
00:25:36.994 --> 00:25:39.872
I just think there's too much delay in…

288
00:25:41.081 --> 00:25:42.207
Uh… Never mind. yeah.

289
00:25:44.376 --> 00:25:45.878
Okay. Should I leave?

290
00:25:58.766 --> 00:26:01.185
Should we take care of that idiot lawyer?

291
00:26:02.144 --> 00:26:04.813
He believes that Jeong Jinman was
the one who attacked us.

292
00:26:06.148 --> 00:26:07.316
I wouldn't worry about it.

293
00:26:07.733 --> 00:26:09.443
[scoffs] I guess.

294
00:26:10.903 --> 00:26:13.781
That lawyer's brain couldn't even
comprehend what went on.

295
00:26:15.657 --> 00:26:18.243
That the reason the bus exploded
that night…

296
00:26:18.869 --> 00:26:22.456
[chuckles] …was to cover up
Bale killing Jun.

297
00:26:33.884 --> 00:26:40.390
Pasin. when we find Atti
and when President Jinman comes back.

298
00:26:42.309 --> 00:26:46.105
can't we all live here together again?

299
00:26:47.773 --> 00:26:51.485
I think it would be… would be nice.

300
00:26:58.867 --> 00:26:59.952
[scoffs]

301
00:27:04.790 --> 00:27:06.750
[♪ ominous music playing]

302
00:27:10.087 --> 00:27:11.713
[Jinman panting]

303
00:27:15.926 --> 00:27:17.636
[mercenary] Mr. Jeong Jinman!

304
00:27:23.225 --> 00:27:25.060
Thanks to you. Mr. Jinman.

305
00:27:25.143 --> 00:27:28.146
Kuma and my team were taken out.
and I got transferred here…

306
00:27:29.064 --> 00:27:30.107
where it's hot as hell.

307
00:27:31.942 --> 00:27:33.068
Ah…

308
00:27:34.111 --> 00:27:36.029
Jo Seonggu. the team leader.

309
00:27:36.446 --> 00:27:38.490
Oh… Thought you forgot.

310
00:27:39.449 --> 00:27:40.450
Well. shoot…

311
00:27:41.201 --> 00:27:43.537
So tell me. Jinman.
why'd you wage a damn war

312
00:27:43.620 --> 00:27:44.872
with Babylon and start this shit?

313
00:27:45.247 --> 00:27:47.541
[groans] Babylon struck first.

314
00:27:48.625 --> 00:27:49.960
I didn't start it.

315
00:27:50.043 --> 00:27:52.337
Makes no difference who started it…

316
00:27:53.797 --> 00:27:56.967
you don't just jump into a battle
you have no chance of winning.

317
00:27:58.927 --> 00:28:03.557
You know. you should've just gone
with the flow. Just like a tree.

318
00:28:04.308 --> 00:28:06.602
If the wind starts blowing.
then you should sway.

319
00:28:07.394 --> 00:28:09.855
Otherwise. you end up taking
the damn beating.

320
00:28:10.772 --> 00:28:11.982
Yeah?

321
00:28:12.065 --> 00:28:17.529
Or else. you'll find yourself like this.
Understand?

322
00:28:20.324 --> 00:28:22.492
-Jo Seonggu.
-What?

323
00:28:23.243 --> 00:28:24.286
Just shut up.

324
00:28:25.954 --> 00:28:28.790
Tell me where Atti is now. I'm in a rush.

325
00:28:30.459 --> 00:28:35.213
Then… I won't kill you
for old times' sake.

326
00:28:41.470 --> 00:28:45.599
Oh. fuck me.
I was about to shit my pants and tell you.

327
00:28:46.892 --> 00:28:48.226
[sighs]

328
00:28:48.560 --> 00:28:49.811
Hey. Jeong Jinman…

329
00:28:51.313 --> 00:28:54.066
you have no idea
what's going on right now. do you?

330
00:28:55.484 --> 00:28:56.652
Just wait a little bit.

331
00:28:57.486 --> 00:29:01.949
I will show you exactly what will happen
to your precious niece and murthehelp.

332
00:29:02.407 --> 00:29:03.867
It's all about to go down.

333
00:29:06.912 --> 00:29:08.455
I hope you're not in pain yet.

334
00:29:09.206 --> 00:29:12.459
Uh-huh. 'Cause from here on.
there's gonna be a lot.

335
00:29:13.710 --> 00:29:15.212
[Seonggu grunts]

336
00:29:16.338 --> 00:29:19.049
[blows thudding]

337
00:29:24.471 --> 00:29:27.349
[Jian] Are we sure they're keeping
Pasin's son in that van?

338
00:29:27.933 --> 00:29:29.226
We never got a picture.

339
00:29:29.309 --> 00:29:33.105
Then that would mean
the mole gave us some false information.

340
00:29:35.023 --> 00:29:36.274
[Pasin] I'll go and handle it.

341
00:29:37.818 --> 00:29:40.195
You need to recover.
you shouldn't go anywhere.

342
00:29:41.780 --> 00:29:43.448
We don't even know if it's accurate.

343
00:29:43.532 --> 00:29:46.868
I have to confirm it. I have to go there.

344
00:29:47.786 --> 00:29:51.164
You guys should… find Jinman quickly.

345
00:29:52.124 --> 00:29:53.125
You should hurry.

346
00:29:55.377 --> 00:29:56.753
If it's to confirm it.

347
00:29:57.713 --> 00:30:00.382
-I think I should go instead.
<i>-Eonni.</i>

348
00:30:00.465 --> 00:30:02.634
[Cheolseung] I don't think
any of us should leave.

349
00:30:02.718 --> 00:30:06.680
It's not a good idea. especially
with the captain missing right now.

350
00:30:07.264 --> 00:30:10.142
Wouldn't it be better to just recruit
a few Code Reds instead?

351
00:30:10.934 --> 00:30:11.935
No.

352
00:30:12.019 --> 00:30:13.645
At the negotiations. they helped us.

353
00:30:13.729 --> 00:30:16.023
but we can't assume
they're on our side yet.

354
00:30:16.106 --> 00:30:17.149
It's too dangerous.

355
00:30:17.232 --> 00:30:20.485
If we move too quickly
and they find out we don't have Jinman.

356
00:30:21.069 --> 00:30:23.488
-they might betray us.
-We're out of time now.

357
00:30:23.572 --> 00:30:24.573
Wait!

358
00:30:27.826 --> 00:30:29.953
The rest of us will hold
the fort down here.

359
00:30:30.662 --> 00:30:33.665
Minhye <i>Eonni</i> can go with Master.
couldn't you?

360
00:30:34.332 --> 00:30:36.668
I think it's too dangerous
to move alone right now.

361
00:30:47.220 --> 00:30:49.473
[K] The shopping mall
is on basement level 2.

362
00:30:49.556 --> 00:30:53.226
They installed cameras operating with
motion sensors throughout the whole area.

363
00:30:53.810 --> 00:30:56.271
If an intruder is detected.
the alarm goes off

364
00:30:56.354 --> 00:30:58.774
and the entire security system activates.

365
00:31:00.692 --> 00:31:02.402
[Jin] He's one crafty bastard.

366
00:31:03.028 --> 00:31:05.822
He knows how we prefer
to keep our operations covert.

367
00:31:07.324 --> 00:31:10.368
He knows that public exposure
would derail our missions.

368
00:31:12.037 --> 00:31:15.207
That's why he built the shopping mall
beneath a site

369
00:31:16.291 --> 00:31:18.460
that's completely full of civilians.

370
00:31:18.543 --> 00:31:20.212
Is this the only exit?

371
00:31:20.921 --> 00:31:22.172
There's no other way out?

372
00:31:22.255 --> 00:31:24.132
That's the only one that we could find.

373
00:31:25.133 --> 00:31:28.929
[Jin] Once our Thai friend does his job
and eliminates So Minhye.

374
00:31:29.012 --> 00:31:30.597
the shopping mall will be ours.

375
00:31:30.680 --> 00:31:33.809
And they'll be defenseless
except for their internal security system.

376
00:31:33.892 --> 00:31:35.602
And Jeong Jinman's where?

377
00:31:37.104 --> 00:31:38.230
Do we know where he is?

378
00:31:38.313 --> 00:31:41.691
Thailand.
We got confirmation of his entry.

379
00:31:42.359 --> 00:31:45.862
We're currently tracking him down
with help from the Thai branch.

380
00:31:46.446 --> 00:31:48.824
[♪ tense plotting music playing]

381
00:31:49.407 --> 00:31:53.578
Once you have Jeong Jian.
that bastard will have no other choice.

382
00:31:53.662 --> 00:31:55.622
Jeong Jinman will come for her.

383
00:31:56.790 --> 00:31:58.041
It's only a matter of time.

384
00:32:01.545 --> 00:32:04.464
-Is it just the four of us going?
-[Jin] No.

385
00:32:04.548 --> 00:32:06.508
Considering our previous attempt…

386
00:32:08.593 --> 00:32:12.055
for this mission.
I will be assigning two teams.

387
00:32:27.612 --> 00:32:30.574
Are you not gonna tell Q
that we already caught Jeong Jinman?

388
00:32:32.284 --> 00:32:34.536
Don't say anything until we catch her.

389
00:32:35.412 --> 00:32:38.498
We need Q to believe
that Jeong Jinman killed J.

390
00:32:38.999 --> 00:32:42.794
She'll put everything
into capturing Jeong Jian. Pow.

391
00:32:43.962 --> 00:32:45.672
[pants and gasps]

392
00:32:46.840 --> 00:32:49.050
[strained grunt]

393
00:32:58.685 --> 00:33:00.645
[groans in pained effort]

394
00:33:05.358 --> 00:33:07.652
[labored panting]

395
00:33:10.238 --> 00:33:12.407
[grunts. pants]

396
00:33:16.995 --> 00:33:18.663
[clanging]

397
00:33:20.165 --> 00:33:21.499
[in Thai] Fuck! Damn!

398
00:33:22.209 --> 00:33:24.169
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

399
00:33:27.631 --> 00:33:29.007
[distant rapid gunfire]

400
00:33:31.635 --> 00:33:34.012
[guns cock]

401
00:33:34.804 --> 00:33:36.806
[gunfire]

402
00:33:41.478 --> 00:33:42.896
[gunfire]

403
00:33:46.691 --> 00:33:47.692
[in English] Go.

404
00:33:54.074 --> 00:33:56.243
[gunfire]

405
00:33:58.078 --> 00:34:00.956
[gunman groaning. screaming]

406
00:34:01.289 --> 00:34:02.582
-[knife slashing]
-[screaming stops]

407
00:34:03.500 --> 00:34:04.793
[Seonggu clicks tongue]

408
00:34:14.344 --> 00:34:17.138
[gunfire]

409
00:34:17.597 --> 00:34:19.140
[Seonggu groans]

410
00:34:20.141 --> 00:34:22.477
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

411
00:34:28.692 --> 00:34:31.069
[screams in pain]

412
00:34:33.280 --> 00:34:34.572
Where are you holding Atti?

413
00:34:36.449 --> 00:34:38.451
I ain't saying shit to you.
you dumb mother--

414
00:34:38.618 --> 00:34:41.204
[Seonggu screams in pain]

415
00:34:50.255 --> 00:34:51.965
You can't kill me. I said where--

416
00:35:18.617 --> 00:35:20.869
[birds screeching]

417
00:35:36.259 --> 00:35:38.345
[♪ tense music playing]

418
00:36:24.307 --> 00:36:25.308
[♪ music fades]

419
00:36:32.315 --> 00:36:33.983
[Pasin] That's where they're holding Atti.

420
00:36:37.612 --> 00:36:38.988
[sighs]

421
00:36:40.532 --> 00:36:42.242
So from here. I'll go on foot.

422
00:36:43.618 --> 00:36:46.913
I'll circle to the back and fire a shot
to draw them in.

423
00:36:48.415 --> 00:36:50.625
After the shot. wait one minute.

424
00:36:50.709 --> 00:36:53.336
Then you hit them from the side
and start the rescue.

425
00:36:59.426 --> 00:37:00.427
Pasin…

426
00:37:02.220 --> 00:37:03.972
I swear. I'll rescue Atti.

427
00:37:07.684 --> 00:37:08.685
[Pasin] Yeah.

428
00:37:10.478 --> 00:37:11.479
Minhye…

429
00:37:14.482 --> 00:37:15.942
thank you for everything.

430
00:37:36.212 --> 00:37:37.547
[phone buzzing]

431
00:37:41.217 --> 00:37:43.303
JIAN - I'M UNEASY ABOUT NOT BEING ABLE
TO REACH MY UNCLE.

432
00:37:43.386 --> 00:37:44.387
YOU BE CAREFUL TOO. MINHYE.

433
00:37:44.471 --> 00:37:46.097
[truck engine revving]

434
00:37:46.181 --> 00:37:48.266
[crashing]

435
00:37:48.349 --> 00:37:50.393
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

436
00:37:54.189 --> 00:37:55.482
[grunts]

437
00:37:57.275 --> 00:37:59.235
[tires screeching]

438
00:38:06.201 --> 00:38:08.077
[grunting. panting]

439
00:38:08.161 --> 00:38:10.038
-[gunshots]
-[glass shatters]

440
00:38:13.500 --> 00:38:15.126
[gasps]

441
00:38:15.710 --> 00:38:17.170
[gunshots]

442
00:38:17.295 --> 00:38:18.838
[groans]

443
00:38:23.092 --> 00:38:25.386
[Minhye grunting]

444
00:38:31.935 --> 00:38:33.311
[Minhye] Pasin…

445
00:38:39.150 --> 00:38:41.444
[gunshots]

446
00:39:09.430 --> 00:39:11.975
[♪ lingering tense music playing]

447
00:39:20.316 --> 00:39:21.818
[line ringing]

448
00:39:23.736 --> 00:39:25.738
I took care of Minhye.

449
00:39:27.782 --> 00:39:31.369
Now… I'll go to the shopping mall.

450
00:39:42.839 --> 00:39:43.840
[♪ music fades]

451
00:40:09.365 --> 00:40:10.992
[lock clanging]

452
00:40:16.331 --> 00:40:18.708
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

453
00:40:28.509 --> 00:40:30.219
[guns cock]

454
00:40:38.061 --> 00:40:39.896
I hired three black-hat hackers

455
00:40:39.979 --> 00:40:43.816
and secured the e-mails exchanged
between Jeong Jinman and his informant.

456
00:40:43.900 --> 00:40:46.069
-[Jin] Do they have what it takes?
-[announcer] <i>Seven. seven.</i>

457
00:40:46.152 --> 00:40:49.364
[K] Yes. They even hacked the NIS before.

458
00:40:49.447 --> 00:40:52.825
[announcer] <i>One-one-zero. one-zero-six…</i>

459
00:40:54.494 --> 00:40:57.163
<i>nine-three. five-zero.</i>

460
00:40:58.873 --> 00:40:59.874
<i>six-nine…</i>

461
00:41:00.458 --> 00:41:02.210
[phone buzzing]

462
00:41:05.505 --> 00:41:06.506
Speak.

463
00:41:10.760 --> 00:41:11.803
Jeong Jinman left?

464
00:41:11.886 --> 00:41:14.347
[yells] Fuck!

465
00:41:14.430 --> 00:41:16.474
[panting]

466
00:41:16.557 --> 00:41:20.186
Tell our Thai branch we need everyone
to prioritize capturing Jeong Jinman.

467
00:41:23.898 --> 00:41:27.026
Q needs to start the mission right away.
We're out of time now.

468
00:41:27.986 --> 00:41:28.987
Tick-tock.

469
00:41:29.988 --> 00:41:30.989
Right away.

470
00:41:32.448 --> 00:41:33.908
[sighs]

471
00:41:34.867 --> 00:41:37.453
-Should I go alone?
-You go ahead.

472
00:41:38.746 --> 00:41:39.789
I'm gonna eat first.

473
00:41:59.308 --> 00:42:02.311
Jian! Jinman's location was sent to us!

474
00:42:05.356 --> 00:42:08.985
You know how. right? The name
and the passport number all match.

475
00:42:09.068 --> 00:42:12.613
You sure
this is actually the mole's message?

476
00:42:13.406 --> 00:42:16.367
Hey. I thought I told you earlier.
only we know the mole's method to…

477
00:42:16.451 --> 00:42:17.452
Look at this.

478
00:42:18.661 --> 00:42:21.789
These are the e-mails the mole sent
my uncle over the past year.

479
00:42:22.957 --> 00:42:24.625
At the end of every subject line…

480
00:42:29.255 --> 00:42:30.465
they put this here.

481
00:42:31.883 --> 00:42:34.177
I think the mole hid it. Now look.

482
00:42:35.928 --> 00:42:38.431
[♪ tense pensive music playing]

483
00:42:41.434 --> 00:42:42.810
They stop here.

484
00:42:52.653 --> 00:42:54.530
[exhales heavily]

485
00:42:54.614 --> 00:42:56.741
It was right in front of us
this whole time.

486
00:42:56.824 --> 00:43:00.453
The last one with the mark was sent
a week ago.

487
00:43:00.536 --> 00:43:04.165
Babylon assholes somehow intercepted it.

488
00:43:21.599 --> 00:43:22.642
Pasin?

489
00:43:23.851 --> 00:43:26.604
What happened? Did you find Atti?

490
00:43:26.687 --> 00:43:27.980
Where is Minhye?

491
00:43:30.942 --> 00:43:32.443
[Jinwoo grunting]

492
00:43:33.444 --> 00:43:35.530
[rhythmic tapping]

493
00:43:42.495 --> 00:43:45.665
[♪ tense music playing]

494
00:43:53.256 --> 00:43:55.174
BABYLON KIDNAPPED PASIN.
POSSIBLE PASIN IS NOW A DOUBLE AGENT.

495
00:43:58.427 --> 00:43:59.637
[Cheolseung] Thai comrade…

496
00:44:01.139 --> 00:44:02.306
what's going on. man?

497
00:44:02.390 --> 00:44:03.516
Are you doing all right?

498
00:44:05.935 --> 00:44:06.936
Where's Minhye?

499
00:44:08.938 --> 00:44:11.732
Master. please tell me.

500
00:44:13.109 --> 00:44:14.902
What'd you do with my uncle and Minhye?

501
00:44:18.114 --> 00:44:20.533
-Jian. get out of here.
-Master!

502
00:44:23.452 --> 00:44:24.954
[Jian groans]

503
00:44:26.038 --> 00:44:27.415
Get the hell out of here!

504
00:44:27.498 --> 00:44:28.791
[Cheolseung groans]

505
00:44:30.168 --> 00:44:31.669
[Jian groans]

506
00:44:34.380 --> 00:44:36.132
[♪ intense suspenseful music playing]

507
00:44:36.215 --> 00:44:37.216
[Jian groans]

508
00:44:38.885 --> 00:44:40.136
[screams]

509
00:44:43.764 --> 00:44:45.850
-[Cheolseung yells]
-[grunting]

510
00:44:55.484 --> 00:44:57.862
[Jian panting]

511
00:44:59.405 --> 00:45:01.741
[both grunting]

512
00:45:04.577 --> 00:45:05.745
[groans]

513
00:45:08.414 --> 00:45:09.582
[grunts]

514
00:45:19.717 --> 00:45:22.178
[♪ intense suspenseful music continues]

515
00:45:31.979 --> 00:45:33.606
[both grunting]

516
00:45:33.689 --> 00:45:35.399
[groans]

517
00:45:35.608 --> 00:45:36.984
[Cheolseung yells]

518
00:45:45.368 --> 00:45:46.369
[♪ music ends]

519
00:45:59.340 --> 00:46:00.925
[device beeps]

520
00:46:03.219 --> 00:46:04.887
[computer beeping]

521
00:46:07.348 --> 00:46:10.476
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

522
00:46:12.895 --> 00:46:14.855
[panting]

523
00:46:17.775 --> 00:46:18.818
What?

524
00:46:20.194 --> 00:46:22.029
[error beeping]

525
00:46:22.196 --> 00:46:24.156
[slams lock]

526
00:46:28.536 --> 00:46:29.537
[Brother] What's…?

527
00:46:43.092 --> 00:46:44.927
[grunts in frustration]

528
00:46:51.225 --> 00:46:53.769
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

529
00:47:00.109 --> 00:47:01.360
Jinwoo?

530
00:47:02.486 --> 00:47:03.738
<i>Cheolseung?</i>

531
00:47:04.697 --> 00:47:06.741
Jeong Jian. where are you?

532
00:47:07.950 --> 00:47:09.952
Pasin's turned on us. We have to go!

533
00:47:10.036 --> 00:47:11.579
What did you say?

534
00:47:11.662 --> 00:47:14.332
There's no time.
I'll explain later. We have to go!

535
00:47:17.918 --> 00:47:21.088
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

536
00:47:31.682 --> 00:47:33.476
Pasin. what are you doing?

537
00:47:33.559 --> 00:47:35.394
[screams] Damn it. Master. what the hell?

538
00:47:48.949 --> 00:47:50.659
Jian…

539
00:47:52.661 --> 00:47:55.873
once you pull out your gun.
you just shoot it. all right?

540
00:47:56.874 --> 00:47:58.959
[Jian yelps. groans]

541
00:48:00.961 --> 00:48:03.839
-Brother! Brother! Brother!
-[Brother groans]

542
00:48:06.675 --> 00:48:07.760
[Jian] Pasin!

543
00:48:08.928 --> 00:48:11.722
Please. what are you doing? Please!

544
00:48:17.144 --> 00:48:20.314
[♪ menacing music playing]

545
00:48:30.032 --> 00:48:31.283
[Jin] <i>Watch carefully.</i>

546
00:48:34.829 --> 00:48:39.166
First. the king.
we separate him from the amateur queen.

547
00:48:40.167 --> 00:48:46.257
Then we take their knight
and turn him into ours. just like this.

548
00:48:46.340 --> 00:48:48.926
And send him in like a Trojan horse.

549
00:48:49.009 --> 00:48:51.804
<i>As for the bishops and pawns</i>
<i>who lost their knight.</i>

550
00:48:51.887 --> 00:48:53.931
just steamroll the whole lot.

551
00:49:02.440 --> 00:49:03.441
[beeping]

552
00:49:06.235 --> 00:49:09.488
Both of the units have been docked.
Initiating the hack.

553
00:49:11.282 --> 00:49:12.533
Thanks for working hard.

554
00:49:15.494 --> 00:49:16.704
[in Japanese] What's the situation?

555
00:49:16.787 --> 00:49:19.498
[in English] We've taken control
of their entire security system now.

556
00:49:19.582 --> 00:49:21.250
We only need to move in.

557
00:49:21.333 --> 00:49:24.837
[in Japanese] Tell Q to eliminate Pasin
once Jeong Jian is captured.

558
00:49:28.132 --> 00:49:30.342
[in English] Then. we go in there…

559
00:49:32.052 --> 00:49:33.179
and capture the queen.

560
00:49:34.180 --> 00:49:36.348
[♪ menacing music continues]

561
00:49:39.852 --> 00:49:44.231
Q. driven by pure revenge.
will capture Jeong Jian.

562
00:49:44.899 --> 00:49:46.525
And once we've taken the queen…

563
00:49:51.197 --> 00:49:54.241
<i>the king is put in endgame.</i>

564
00:49:54.325 --> 00:49:59.121
A SHOP FOR KILLERS 2

565
00:50:00.039 --> 00:50:01.040
[♪ music ends]

566
00:50:18.390 --> 00:50:19.850
[Jin] Korean barbecue?

567
00:50:20.059 --> 00:50:22.394
[groans] The smell's gonna stick.

568
00:50:24.146 --> 00:50:25.147
[exhales]

569
00:50:26.899 --> 00:50:29.443
Oh. wow. [chuckles]

570
00:50:30.903 --> 00:50:32.738
I always wanted to meet you in person.

571
00:50:32.821 --> 00:50:34.281
I know it looks shabby. but…

572
00:50:35.366 --> 00:50:39.203
Our meat here is out of this world.
So that's why I invited you.

573
00:50:44.750 --> 00:50:45.960
Hm?

574
00:50:47.920 --> 00:50:51.048
[♪ tense pensive music playing]

575
00:50:55.761 --> 00:50:57.179
Ahn Seongbeom.

576
00:50:58.514 --> 00:50:59.515
It's a pleasure.

577
00:51:02.226 --> 00:51:05.187
[♪ closing theme music playing]

578
00:51:08.065 --> 00:51:09.525
BASED ON THE NOVEL BY KANG JI YOUNG

579
